        "original_id": "482ab452-e4b3-50bd-98fb-6b0cd44ac2de",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Charts: Canadian Hot 100\n- Publications: Billboard\n- Music release types: Single\n- Songs: Is Anybody Out There?\n\nFacts:\n- The Canadian Hot 100 is a singles record chart in Canada that is published weekly by Billboard magazine.\n- A single, also called a record single or music single, is a music release that typically contains fewer tracks than an LP, album, or EP.\n- A single is usually released separately from an album, although it often also appears on an album.\n- The song \"Is Anybody Out There?\" debuted at number 67 on the Canadian Hot 100 and later peaked at number 14.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
